def sort_by_dnf(arr, n):
    low, mid, high = 0, 0, n - 1

    while mid <= high:
        if arr[mid] == 0:
            arr[low], arr[mid] = arr[mid], arr[low]
            low += 1
            mid += 1
        elif arr[mid] == 1:
            mid += 1
        else:
            arr[mid], arr[high] = arr[high], arr[mid]
            high -= 1

    return arr
```

This solution sorts the array in O(n) time complexity and O(1) space complexity. It uses a three-pointer approach to partition the array into three parts: 0s, 1s, and 2s. The pointers `low`, `mid`, and `high` are used to traverse the array and rearrange the elements accordingly.

