def largest_subset(nums, n):
    # Sort the list to make finding the largest subset easier
    nums.sort()

    # Initialize a DP array where dp[i] represents the length of the largest subset ending at index i
    dp = [1] * n

    # Iterate through the list to fill the DP array
    for i in range(1, n):
        # Check all previous elements to find a pair that is divisible
        for j in range(i):
            if nums[i] % nums[j] == 0 and dp[i] < dp[j] + 1:
                dp[i] = dp[j] + 1

    # The length of the largest subset found will be the maximum value in dp
    return max(dp)
```

This function uses dynamic programming to find the largest subset where each pair of elements is divisible. It sorts the list first to ensure that we can easily check divisibility and construct the subset. The DP array is initialized to 1 for each element, as each element itself forms a trivial subset. The function then iterates through the list, updating the DP array based on the maximum length of subsets that include the current element. Finally, it returns the maximum value in the DP array, which represents the length of the largest divisible subset.

